{"record": "turn", "turn": 7, "seconds": 3.463, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2831}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2831, "cache_read_input_tokens": 18297, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 526, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 28}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_017E2rQq3GAUZjwu2PE8Hw7E", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"found": false, "answer": "The paper does not quote a detection significance (in σ or as a test statistic) for the GCE in its 17.7-year analysis. I read the Introduction, Template Fitting, Systematic Uncertainties and DM interpretation sections and the Conclusions. Section 3.5 says only that the fitted GCE flux is nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, and that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance\". It adds that the differences in Δ(−2lnL) between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The paper does give Δ(−2lnL) values for the next-best diffuse models relative to Model X: 72.1, 149.7, 487.9, 517.5 and 638.2 for LIII, XV, XLI, VII and XLVII. These compare diffuse-emission models and are not a GCE detection significance. I did not read the remaining sections (2, 3.1–3.3, 4–7 and the appendices) in full.", "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "8"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261120T065830Z_dev-05_staged_67b4", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"found": false, "answer": "The paper does not quote a detection significance (in σ or as a test statistic) for the GCE in its 17.7-year analysis. I read the Introduction, Template Fitting, Systematic Uncertainties and DM interpretation sections and the Conclusions. Section 3.5 says only that the fitted GCE flux is nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, and that this \"alone does not establish its statistical significance\". It adds that the differences in Δ(−2lnL) between the non-nested diffuse models cannot be read as squared Gaussian significances. The paper does give Δ(−2lnL) values for the next-best diffuse models relative to Model X: 72.1, 149.7, 487.9, 517.5 and 638.2 for LIII, XV, XLI, VII and XLVII. These compare diffuse-emission models and are not a GCE detection significance. I did not read the remaining sections (2, 3.1–3.3, 4–7 and the appendices) in full.", "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "8"}]}, "turns": 7, "seconds": 12.853, "tool_calls": 9, "tool_result_chars": 42562, "input_tokens": 16, "output_tokens": 1404, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11838, "cache_read_input_tokens": 70066, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-20T06:58:43+00:00"}
